James received an email from Rohit Dongre, a prospective Ph.D. candidate for the Environmental Economics program at the University of Delaware. Rohit detailed his impressive educational background, including a Bachelor’s in Mechanical Engineering and a Master’s in Economics, along with fieldwork experiences in Costa Rica and Uganda. He expressed his interest in topics such as pollution control using smog tower technology and the impact of caste on marginalized communities in India. James acknowledged Rohit's qualifications and interests but informed him that he does not have funding to accept new Ph.D. students this year. He encouraged Rohit to schedule a Zoom chat if he desired further discussion or advice regarding his research interests.
